Preamble

CERN has developed this licence to promote collaboration among
hardware designers and to provide a legal tool which supports the
freedom to use, study, modify, make and distribute hardware designs
and products based on those designs.

Version 2 of the CERN Open Hardware Licence comes in three variants:
CERN-OHL-P (permissive); and two reciprocal licences: this licence,
CERN-OHL-S (strongly reciprocal), and CERN-OHL-W (weakly reciprocal).

The full licence text is available at:
https://ohwr.org/project/cernohl/wikis/Documents/CERN-OHL-version-2

Summary of key conditions:

1. You may use, copy, modify and distribute this hardware design and
   products made from it, for any purpose, commercially or not.

2. If you distribute modified versions of the design, or products
   made from modified designs, you must:
   - Release the modified design under this same licence (CERN-OHL-S v2)
   - Make all design source files available
   - Clearly indicate what you have changed

3. You must retain all copyright, licence, and attribution notices.

4. Attribution: Joy Bose, 2026. Assisted Prostration Device (APD).
   github.com/[username]/apd-prostration-device

For the complete licence text, see:
https://ohwr.org/cern_ohl_s_v2.txt
